AdGuard Home on FenrirOS
========================

Installed inert: the service is not enabled, there is no configuration and
no account.

    dinitctl enable adguardhome

On first start (no /var/lib/adguardhome/AdGuardHome.yaml) it serves its setup
wizard on http://<host>:3000 on every interface; whoever opens it first
chooses the admin account, the web and DNS ports. Do this at once, on a
trusted network. It runs as the adguardhome user with the capabilities to
bind ports below 1024 (DNS on 53) and to use raw sockets (its DHCP server).
Anything else listening on port 53 (dnsmasq, unbound, a local resolver) must
be moved or stopped first.

Self-update is turned off (--no-check-update in /etc/dinit.d/adguardhome):
updates come from the package. It downloads the filter lists you choose
from their publishers; "Send anonymous statistics" does not exist in it.
